---
pagination:
  data: redirects
  size: 1
  alias: r
redirects:
  - { from: "/schedule/", to: "/program/" }
  - { from: "/accessibility/", to: "/join/#interpretation" }
  - { from: "/meeting/", to: "/principles/" }
permalink: "{{ r.from }}"
layout: false
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Pages that moved in the October 2026 redesign. GitHub Pages has no server-side redirects, so each
    old address is a tiny page that forwards at once and names the new page as its canonical, so search
    engines move the old address over (no noindex, which would contradict the canonical; the stubs are
    already left out of the sitemap). -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ site.name }}</title>
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ r.to | absUrl }}">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ r.to }}">
</head>
<body>
<p>This page has moved: <a href="{{ r.to }}">{{ r.to | absUrl }}</a></p>
</body>
</html>
